Golden Pills use the recharge time of the pill they mimicked. Recharge time is unaffected by whether or not it was a normal pill or Horse Pill.

Note that because the recharge time is determined after using the pill, Placebo cannot be used as a way to narrow down what type of pill Isaac is holding before he uses it.

== Synergies ==
* [[Pills#Pill Effects|48 Hour Energy]]:
** {{dlc|nr}} Can spawn an unlimited number of {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, allowing unlimited use of another activated item or pill.
** {{dlc|r}} One battery is guaranteed to be a {{E|Lil' Battery}}, any additional batteries spawn as {{E|Micro Battery|text=Micro Batteries}}. The item does not recharge upon use.
** '''Placebo''' + {{I|Car Battery}}: Both batteries are guaranteed to be {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, any additional batteries spawn as {{E|Micro Battery|text=Micro Batteries}}, once again allowing unlimited usage.
*** {{P|IX - The Hermit?}} can be used to "sell" any and all {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}} and {{E|Micro Battery|text=Micro Batteries}} for 5 Pennies each, effectively allowing for in instant max of coins, provided you have spawned The Hermit? in another room, or have it in your second slot with {{I|Polydactyly}}.
**** + {{I|Schoolbag}} + {{I|Blank Card}}: Effectively an extremely complicated method of producing infinite money.
* {{dlc|nr}} [[Pills#Pill Effects|Balls of Steel]] + {{i|Sharp Plug}}: Allows functional invincibility.
** {{dlc|nr}} {{i|The Wafer}}: Allows for virtually infinite health.
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns white wisps on the middle ring. The wisps spawn [[pill]]s when destroyed. The effects of the wisps and types of pills they spawn is independent from Placebo's charge time and the most recently used pill. Unlike {{I|Blank Card}} and {{I|Clear Rune}}, enemies killed by these wisps' tears do not have a chance to drop pills.}}
* {{dlc|r}} [[Pills#Pill Effects|Vurp]]: Allows pills that normally take 12 rooms for Placebo to charge to be used twice as frequently.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Starter Deck}}: All pills are replaced by cards, rendering Placebo useless.
** {{dlc|r}} '''Starter Deck''' + {{i|Little Baggy}}: Both cards and pills can be encountered again.

